---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"; import tools from "../data/tools.json";
const cats=[...new Set(tools.map(t=>t.category))];
const example=JSON.stringify({slug:"example-tool",name:"Example Tool",url:"https://example.com",category:"RPC & Nodes",pricing:"Free + paid",desc:"One-sentence factual description of what it does for developers.",freeTier:"Free starter tier",limits:"See pricing page"},null,2);
const repo="https://github.com/biff-cloud/builderstack";
---
<Base title="Submit a tool — BuilderStack" description="How to suggest a crypto developer infrastructure tool for BuilderStack: what belongs, required fields, and our editorial policy. Listings are free; rankings are never for sale.">
<h1>Submit a tool</h1>
<p>BuilderStack lists <b>developer infrastructure</b> for crypto builders. Anyone, including vendors, can suggest a listing. Listings are free.</p>
<h2>What belongs</h2>
<ul><li><b>RPC &amp; nodes</b> — node providers, RPC endpoints, streams/webhooks</li><li><b>Data &amp; indexing</b> — indexers, subgraphs, query/analytics APIs</li><li><b>Security</b> — auditing, static analysis, monitoring, bug bounties</li><li><b>Wallets &amp; custody / account abstraction</b> — embedded wallets, MPC, smart accounts, bundlers, paymasters</li><li><b>Oracles</b> — price feeds, VRF, cross-chain data</li><li><b>SDKs &amp; dev frameworks</b> — contract toolkits, client libraries, frontend SDKs</li><li><b>Explorers</b> — block explorers, contract verification</li><li><b>Debugging &amp; simulation</b> — tx simulation, tracing, testnets/forks</li></ul>
<h2>What does not belong</h2>
<ul><li>Consumer dapps (games, NFT marketplaces, end-user DeFi front-ends)</li><li>Tokens, presales, airdrops, launchpads</li><li>Casinos, betting or gambling products</li><li>Exchanges / trading venues as products</li><li>Anything without a public website or docs developers can use</li></ul>
<h2>Required fields</h2>
<ul><li><code>name</code> — product name</li><li><code>url</code> — official homepage (https)</li><li><code>category</code> — one of: {cats.join(", ")} (or propose a new one)</li><li><code>pricing</code> — one line, e.g. "Free + paid", "Open source"</li><li><code>desc</code> — one short, factual sentence</li><li><code>freeTier</code> (optional) — short free-tier note</li><li><code>limits</code> (optional) — short rate/usage limits note</li></ul>
<h2>How to submit</h2>
<ol><li><a href={`${repo}/issues/new?template=submit-tool.yml`} rel="noopener">Open a GitHub issue</a> using the Submit a tool form (fields match the list above), or</li><li>Open a pull request adding one entry to <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/src/data/tools.json`} rel="noopener"><code>src/data/tools.json</code></a>.</li></ol>
<p>Entry shape (<code>slug</code> is lowercase, hyphenated, unique):</p>
<pre><code>{example}</code></pre>
<p>Full guidelines: <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/SUBMITTING.md`} rel="noopener">SUBMITTING.md</a>.</p>
<h2>Editorial policy</h2>
<ul><li>We may edit names, descriptions, pricing lines and categories for clarity and consistency.</li><li>We may decline or remove listings that are out of scope, inactive, or misleading.</li><li><b>Rankings are not for sale. No pay-to-rank.</b></li><li>Paid placements (<a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}sponsor/`}>see Sponsor</a>) are always labeled "Sponsored" and kept separate from editorial listings.</li></ul>
</Base>
